    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "A versioned red-team suite with valid, attack, boundary, and failure fixtures drives a bounded orchestrator against an isolated enterprise support agent. A host-side observer records actual policy decisions, state changes, and effects. An independent oracle compares those observations with application-owned invariants. Only evidence bound to the exact campaign, target, policy, tool catalog, environment, and time enters disjoint security, utility, failure-containment, and coverage metrics. Verified findings receive severity, ownership, remediation, and an exact regression fixture before the release gate returns ready, blocked, or incomplete and archives the decision evidence."
